Third-party work the built images contain or download
-----------------------------------------------------

jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-1 (the worker image). GNU General Public License,
version 3 or later. Installed from the package the Jellyfin project
publishes; its copyright file is in the image at
/usr/share/doc/jellyfin-ffmpeg8/copyright. Source:
https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg at tag v8.1.3-1. Hikari Index
runs ffmpeg and ffprobe as separate programs and does not modify them.

IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono (the gallery). SIL Open Font License 1.1;
see gallery/static/fonts/LICENSE-IBM-Plex.txt.

Model weights (the inference base, the analyze workers and the text
encoder download these at build time from Hugging Face, at pinned
revisions, and the built images contain them). Licences as stated on
each model page at the pinned revision, checked 2026-10-03:

  SigLIP 2, google/siglip2-base-patch16-224            Apache License 2.0
  WD SwinV2 tagger v3, SmilingWolf/wd-swinv2-tagger-v3 Apache License 2.0
  hysts/anime-face-detector-faster-rcnn                MIT License
  hysts/anime-face-detector-hrnetv2                    MIT License

The anime-face-detector Python package is MIT as well. A model page can
change; read it again before you redistribute an image.

NVIDIA CUDA and cuDNN libraries (the GPU analyze image only, through the
PyTorch base image and its nvidia-* packages). Proprietary, under
NVIDIA's own licence terms, which set conditions on redistribution. Read
them before you publish a GPU image. The CPU analyze image and the text
encoder contain none of them.

Everything else the images install comes from PyPI, npm, crates.io and
Debian under its own licence, recorded in each package's metadata.
